.TH PATH_BASENAME2 3
.SH NAME
path_basename2 \- return a pointer to the basename of a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "char* path_basename2(const char* " path ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_basename2
calculates the position of the final component (basename) of the path provided in
.I path
with length
.IR len .
.PP
The function identifies the last occurrence of the system's path separator and returns a pointer to the character immediately following it. If the path contains no separators, the original pointer is returned.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the start of the basename within the original
.I path
buffer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_basepos2 (3)